# Deliberately empty of fingerprints.
#
# A gitleaks fingerprint is <file>:<rule>:<startline>, so it stops matching
# the moment the suppressed line moves, and the scan silently starts failing
# (or, worse, a genuinely new finding lands on the old line number and is
# suppressed). The one reviewed non-secret finding, the RFC 6455 sample
# WebSocket nonce in internal/api/ws_test.go, is allowlisted in
# .gitleaks.toml by file and by exact value instead, which cannot drift.
#
# Add a fingerprint here only for a finding that cannot be pinned to a stable
# file-and-value pair, and say why. Anything that can be expressed as a
# targetRules allowlist in .gitleaks.toml belongs there.
